WEBVTT

1
00:48:54.530 --> 00:49:02.490
Does everyone have a spot? No? Is anyone in agreement that we need a new church building?

2
00:49:02.490 --> 00:49:09.490
Can I hear an amen to that? Really, right? At the same time, we are grateful for this building.

3
00:49:09.490 --> 00:49:16.250
What a blessing. God is a God of blessing upon blessing, step by step. Did you know that?

4
00:49:16.250 --> 00:49:23.290
He takes care of us every step. And you know, God wants to take us through life.

5
00:49:23.290 --> 00:49:31.250
He can give us everything at any moment. But the question is, do we have a walk together with Him in faith upon faith?

6
00:49:31.250 --> 00:49:34.410
Do you understand what I mean? Praise God.

7
00:49:34.410 --> 00:49:40.090
Are there people here for the first time in Open Church today? Give a wave if you are visiting us.

8
00:49:40.090 --> 00:49:48.130
There are people. Can we give a round of applause for our guests? Thank you for being here.

9
00:49:48.130 --> 00:49:57.130
Where are you from? Bladel. The Lord died for that too. For Bladel. Awesome, thank you.

10
00:49:57.130 --> 00:50:06.610
That's true. And how did you get here? Good. Me too. But Jesus died for that. Amen?

11
00:50:06.610 --> 00:50:14.810
Praise the Lord. Hallelujah. The Bible says, whoever is set free by the Lord is truly free. Truly free.

12
00:50:14.810 --> 00:50:20.090
So I, when I was addicted and still walking in the world, I had two choices.

13
00:50:20.090 --> 00:50:26.370
Either continue in that nonsense I was living in, or move forward with Jesus. And I am free. I am totally free.

14
00:50:26.370 --> 00:50:30.850
Nothing more, no alcohol, no drugs, nothing more, no porn. Completely free.

15
00:50:30.850 --> 00:50:36.410
Whoever is set free by the Lord is truly free. Amen? Amen.

16
00:50:36.410 --> 00:50:40.090
Praise the Lord. Hallelujah.

17
00:50:40.090 --> 00:50:47.690
I hope you came for Jesus and not for the international food of a service.

18
00:50:47.690 --> 00:50:55.210
Yes, that’s fine too. Oh my gosh, how good it will be in heaven. All kinds of places.

19
00:50:55.210 --> 00:51:01.210
If you are looking for me in heaven, I will be in the Indonesian corner. That’s where you can find me. Seriously.

20
00:51:01.210 --> 00:51:05.850
I was just born in the wrong skin. I love it. Seriously.

21
00:51:05.850 --> 00:51:12.490
Praise the Lord. Listen, I want to share something with you all. I want to discuss the collections with you today.

22
00:51:12.490 --> 00:51:19.370
And very often we teach from God's Word that it is good for us to bring our tithes to the congregation.

23
00:51:19.370 --> 00:51:23.770
So that we can build up money in the congregation, so that we can buy a new building.

24
00:51:23.770 --> 00:51:29.530
So that we can pay the salaries, so that we can simply function as a church.

25
00:51:29.530 --> 00:51:36.330
And I am an advocate of giving tithes. Ever since I have known Jesus, I have given 10% of my income.

26
00:51:36.330 --> 00:51:41.770
So even now as a pastor, while I receive a salary from the church, I give 10% to the church.

27
00:51:41.770 --> 00:51:47.770
Because I believe in giving 10%. I believe that this blesses me.

28
00:51:47.770 --> 00:51:51.370
And I believe that God asks this from His Word.

29
00:51:51.370 --> 00:51:57.370
Now it is a law from the Old Testament that it must be, that it must be, that it must be, otherwise God will strike you.

30
00:51:57.530 --> 00:52:03.130
No, I no longer think it works that way. I believe that under the cross, what the prophet Joel has said,

31
00:52:03.130 --> 00:52:09.930
that a time will come when it is no longer a law that must be, but that it will be a law written in your heart.

32
00:52:09.930 --> 00:52:15.290
So I do not give my tithes because it must be, that it must be, and otherwise the church will impose a sanction on you.

33
00:52:15.290 --> 00:52:18.090
But I give 10% because I love Jesus.

34
00:52:18.090 --> 00:52:26.890
In the letter to the Hebrews, New Testament, it says that in the Old Testament they gave the tithes to the high priest, Melchizedek.

35
00:52:26.890 --> 00:52:32.170
But in the New Testament we give the tithes to the high, high priest and His name is Jesus.

36
00:52:32.170 --> 00:52:38.970
So I believe as a New Testament believer that I personally give my tithes to the church to Jesus.

37
00:52:38.970 --> 00:52:42.250
And I have always given my tithes and I have never been in lack.

38
00:52:42.250 --> 00:52:47.370
There have been evenings when I had to go eat at my parents' house because there was too little to be found in my own fridge

39
00:52:47.370 --> 00:52:51.850
to cook a decent meal, but that does not mean that I had too little.

40
00:52:51.850 --> 00:52:58.890
Jesus always takes care of you. Can I get an amen on that?

41
00:52:58.890 --> 00:53:02.810
All right, but I don't want to talk about that today during the collection.

42
00:53:02.810 --> 00:53:09.210
Look, very often we as a church talk about finances and that we want to continue as a church and that it is important that we do this

43
00:53:09.210 --> 00:53:15.530
so that we can grow, so that the people in the Kempen can come to Jesus and that we can disciple them in the name of Jesus.

44
00:53:15.530 --> 00:53:17.290
Super important topic.

45
00:53:17.290 --> 00:53:24.330
What I want to talk about today is poverty and how we rich people should look at poverty from the Bible.

46
00:53:24.330 --> 00:53:31.530
Because there are indeed many Bible verses that speak about giving money to the poor.

47
00:53:31.530 --> 00:53:37.210
And the church must not ignore this. On the contrary, the Western church must certainly not ignore this.

48
00:53:37.210 --> 00:53:41.130
If the Western church ignores this, we sin against God.

49
00:53:41.130 --> 00:53:45.290
For God did not make us rich to be rich ourselves, who knows this.

50
00:53:45.290 --> 00:53:50.570
God did not give us wealth so that we can be well off ourselves while everyone else can struggle.

51
00:53:50.570 --> 00:53:54.730
That is not how it works in the kingdom of God. In the world, it is like that.

52
00:53:54.730 --> 00:54:01.130
But in God's kingdom, we live in sacrifice for what the Lord has made. Amen?

53
00:54:01.130 --> 00:54:08.330
Here is a Bible verse that has been significant to me for many years; since I first read it, I have marked it in my Bible.

54
00:54:08.330 --> 00:54:11.370
Because I find it a very important Bible verse.

55
00:54:11.450 --> 00:54:14.890
The book of Proverbs is for me one of the great books of the Bible.

56
00:54:14.890 --> 00:54:20.810
If you want to become wiser, read a proverb daily. Even if it's just one. Even if it's just one chapter.

57
00:54:20.810 --> 00:54:23.850
But those proverbs simply give more and more wisdom.

58
00:54:23.850 --> 00:54:30.650
And here in Proverbs chapter 19, verse 17, it says the following words. Just look at the screen.

59
00:54:30.650 --> 00:54:38.090
If you give something to a poor person, you are lending it to the Lord.

60
00:54:38.090 --> 00:54:44.170
He will repay you by rewarding you for it.

61
00:54:44.170 --> 00:54:51.530
Okay, now we can look at this Bible verse in terms of looking at profit.

62
00:54:51.530 --> 00:54:55.930
So if I give to a poor person, then the Lord will reward me for it.

63
00:54:55.930 --> 00:54:59.770
So if I give to a poor person, then I will soon receive a new car from the Lord.

64
00:54:59.770 --> 00:55:05.210
But I personally want to step away from this kind of gospel.

65
00:55:05.290 --> 00:55:09.690
I'm not really a fan of the prosperity gospel.

66
00:55:09.690 --> 00:55:14.490
I know this has often been the case in the church. I believe that God takes care of me.

67
00:55:14.490 --> 00:55:19.850
I believe that I am rich. I believe that I have everything and more than what I need.

68
00:55:19.850 --> 00:55:24.890
But I also believe that Jesus wants to say that we should give to the poor.

69
00:55:24.890 --> 00:55:30.010
Not so that God can reward us. He will reward us. He will take care of you.

70
00:55:30.090 --> 00:55:35.290
But the Bible says we must give to poor people. Period. Right?

71
00:55:35.290 --> 00:55:38.410
And Open Church has always done this as a model.

72
00:55:38.410 --> 00:55:44.090
We have always given money to Haiti. We have always given money to Madagascar.

73
00:55:44.090 --> 00:55:49.210
We have always given money to Iran. By the way, you shouldn't do that in your bank transfer.

74
00:55:49.210 --> 00:55:53.050
You get a red flag, and your bank account gets frozen. Don't do that quickly.

75
00:55:53.050 --> 00:55:58.090
But we have always given money to causes where the money was needed.

76
00:55:58.170 --> 00:56:02.810
Also during the Covid period, where poor families in Lommel themselves,

77
00:56:02.810 --> 00:56:05.850
because we often think that poverty is in a third world country,

78
00:56:05.850 --> 00:56:08.970
but poverty can also be here in our own area.

79
00:56:08.970 --> 00:56:13.210
That is why we have an organization in Open Church called Open Area.

80
00:56:13.210 --> 00:56:19.530
So that we can collect money and tackle poverty initiatives in our own area.

81
00:56:19.530 --> 00:56:26.330
I spoke yesterday with a couple at the football club, who said that they are still recovering now

82
00:56:26.330 --> 00:56:29.290
from the energy crisis a few years ago.

83
00:56:29.290 --> 00:56:34.890
That energy crisis caused their energy bill, their energy invoice,

84
00:56:34.890 --> 00:56:39.130
to go from 300 euros per month to 1400 euros per month.

85
00:56:39.130 --> 00:56:40.810
And they said, we simply didn't have that money.

86
00:56:40.810 --> 00:56:44.650
Our savings just went away and we are still recovering from that.

87
00:56:44.650 --> 00:56:48.650
So poverty can also happen in our own area.

88
00:56:48.650 --> 00:56:55.690
And I believe that as a church it is our responsibility to engage ourselves in poverty.

89
00:56:55.770 --> 00:56:57.850
We give eggs to the food bank.

90
00:56:57.850 --> 00:56:59.210
Eggs? Yes, eggs.

91
00:56:59.210 --> 00:57:03.930
Because these are important vitamin bombs, also for poor people who cannot afford eggs.

92
00:57:03.930 --> 00:57:05.690
Eggs are expensive.

93
00:57:05.690 --> 00:57:07.370
Then you think to yourself, what a strange product.

94
00:57:07.370 --> 00:57:11.210
Yes, it is a strange product, but it is indeed a divine product.

95
00:57:11.210 --> 00:57:13.130
And we simply give eggs to poor people.

96
00:57:13.130 --> 00:57:17.530
But I also want to give you a piece of teaching today.

97
00:57:17.530 --> 00:57:24.490
That you too should take care of a piece of poverty in your life.

98
00:57:24.570 --> 00:57:28.490
In the past two weeks, Vanessa and I went on a short vacation with the children.

99
00:57:28.490 --> 00:57:30.570
To catch some sun for a while.

100
00:57:30.570 --> 00:57:36.170
And on our way back yesterday, or the day before yesterday, we were driving home.

101
00:57:36.170 --> 00:57:39.850
I love to drive at three o'clock at night.

102
00:57:39.850 --> 00:57:42.970
I had made some pasta salad.

103
00:57:42.970 --> 00:57:46.490
Because on those highways, they only sell junk food.

104
00:57:46.490 --> 00:57:48.010
Don't eat that stuff.

105
00:57:48.010 --> 00:57:52.890
And so I had made a container of pasta salad with some cherry tomatoes.

106
00:57:52.890 --> 00:57:54.170
Because I love good food.

107
00:57:54.170 --> 00:57:56.170
Parmesan cheese, sausages in it.

108
00:57:56.170 --> 00:57:57.130
Just delicious.

109
00:57:57.130 --> 00:57:59.530
And I put that in a bag and I drive home.

110
00:57:59.530 --> 00:58:02.650
And I drive the full twelve hours straight through.

111
00:58:02.650 --> 00:58:04.090
God bless coffee.

112
00:58:04.090 --> 00:58:09.130
And at one point, just as we entered Belgium.

113
00:58:09.130 --> 00:58:14.250
So you leave France, you go through Luxembourg and then you just enter Belgium.

114
00:58:14.250 --> 00:58:17.610
And there I stopped for a moment at a parking lot.

115
00:58:17.610 --> 00:58:22.090
And all of a sudden, I was just eating and I was minding my own business.

116
00:58:22.090 --> 00:58:24.650
And suddenly from the bushes came a man.

117
00:58:24.650 --> 00:58:28.010
And he walked up to me and said...

118
00:58:28.010 --> 00:58:31.290
Yes, in English he said, do you have something to drink for me?

119
00:58:31.290 --> 00:58:36.170
Because I have no home and I am hungry and do you perhaps have something to drink for me?

120
00:58:36.170 --> 00:58:36.970
And here it went.

121
00:58:36.970 --> 00:58:39.290
So I had my bag there.

122
00:58:39.290 --> 00:58:42.170
So I take out of my bag, I take a can.

123
00:58:42.170 --> 00:58:43.530
I had a can of Cola Zero.

124
00:58:43.530 --> 00:58:44.650
You shouldn't really drink that, but okay.

125
00:58:44.650 --> 00:58:46.490
I had a can of Cola Zero.

126
00:58:46.490 --> 00:58:48.250
And I said to him, here you go.

127
00:58:48.250 --> 00:58:50.250
That's what he asked for.

128
00:58:50.250 --> 00:58:52.490
And he said, oh thank you, thank you, thank you.

129
00:58:52.490 --> 00:58:53.690
And he walked away.

130
00:58:53.690 --> 00:58:59.450
And I immediately had an instant feeling of, yes, but this is not a sacrifice.

131
00:58:59.450 --> 00:59:01.050
This is not a sacrifice at all.

132
00:59:01.050 --> 00:59:02.410
Because I'll tell you even stronger.

133
00:59:02.410 --> 00:59:05.210
I'm sure I wouldn't have drunk that can that day.

134
00:59:05.210 --> 00:59:08.090
It would probably have disappeared into our own fridge.

135
00:59:08.090 --> 00:59:13.050
It would probably have been drunk by those two freeloaders who live in my house.

136
00:59:13.050 --> 00:59:15.610
So no sacrifice, not at all.

137
00:59:15.610 --> 00:59:17.450
And it bothered me.

138
00:59:17.530 --> 00:59:19.850
And he walked away.

139
00:59:19.850 --> 00:59:22.410
And I was like, ah, ah.

140
00:59:22.410 --> 00:59:27.930
And so I grab one of those containers, one of those Tupperware containers with the pasta salad.

141
00:59:27.930 --> 00:59:29.930
And I was looking for where is he?

142
00:59:29.930 --> 00:59:33.450
And I run after him to also give him my pasta salad.

143
00:59:33.450 --> 00:59:34.650
And I give it to him.

144
00:59:34.650 --> 00:59:37.850
And he said, oh thank you so much, thank you so much.

145
00:59:37.850 --> 00:59:39.450
And I walk away.

146
00:59:39.450 --> 00:59:43.370
And still I felt, but this is still not a sacrifice.

147
00:59:43.370 --> 00:59:45.050
I am still overweight.

148
00:59:45.450 --> 00:59:48.890
Still I can afford to just give that away.

149
00:59:48.890 --> 00:59:50.490
Who cares?

150
00:59:50.490 --> 00:59:54.170
So I run after him again and I give him a stack of cookies.

151
00:59:54.170 --> 00:59:57.770
I say, yes here please, eat that as well.

152
00:59:57.770 --> 01:00:00.730
And again, oh thank you so much, thank you so much.

153
01:00:00.730 --> 01:00:02.650
And I said to him, what happened in life?

154
01:00:02.650 --> 01:00:05.850
What happened in your life that you ended up here?

155
01:00:05.850 --> 01:00:11.530
In rich Europe, why are you walking around here with a yoga mat?

156
01:00:11.530 --> 01:00:14.410
And he said, man, stuff happened man.

157
01:00:14.410 --> 01:00:16.810
Life has just been tough, he said.

158
01:00:16.810 --> 01:00:19.930
Difficult choices, wrong choices made.

159
01:00:19.930 --> 01:00:23.450
And now he is walking through Europe looking for a better chance.

160
01:00:23.450 --> 01:00:25.050
I say, where are you from?

161
01:00:25.050 --> 01:00:26.890
He said, I come from Northern Germany.

162
01:00:26.890 --> 01:00:29.450
I have completely descended towards Italy.

163
01:00:29.450 --> 01:00:31.530
And now I am on my way back to Brussels.

164
01:00:31.530 --> 01:00:34.730
And I said to him, there is nothing to be found in Brussels either, mate.

165
01:00:34.730 --> 01:00:36.410
Fair is fair.

166
01:00:36.410 --> 01:00:39.290
Because life sucks for some people.

167
01:00:39.290 --> 01:00:40.330
Really, I mean it.

168
01:00:40.330 --> 01:00:42.570
Jesus is the way, the truth, and the life.

169
01:00:42.570 --> 01:00:45.530
And there is only Jesus, Jesus, Jesus.

170
01:00:45.530 --> 01:00:47.850
And even then it can sometimes be difficult.

171
01:00:47.850 --> 01:00:52.170
There are people in this church who have to turn every penny.

172
01:00:52.170 --> 01:00:56.730
And I just felt that God was saying to me,

173
01:00:56.730 --> 01:00:59.210
that can of drink was no sacrifice.

174
01:00:59.210 --> 01:01:01.290
That pasta salad was no sacrifice.

175
01:01:01.290 --> 01:01:03.770
Those three luwkoekjes were no sacrifice.

176
01:01:03.770 --> 01:01:05.610
It is still just not a sacrifice.

177
01:01:05.610 --> 01:01:10.330
You have to do something about poverty in your life.

178
01:01:10.330 --> 01:01:11.610
I don't care what you do.

179
01:01:11.690 --> 01:01:13.050
I will just leave it at that.

180
01:01:13.050 --> 01:01:15.770
This is the teaching I want to give you during this collection.

181
01:01:15.770 --> 01:01:17.530
So don't give your money to Open Church.

182
01:01:17.530 --> 01:01:20.730
But take some time this week to think about what you can do.

183
01:01:21.290 --> 01:01:22.250
There is compassion.

184
01:01:22.250 --> 01:01:25.130
You can adopt a child through compassion.

185
01:01:25.130 --> 01:01:27.770
Are there people in this room who have a compassion child?

186
01:01:27.770 --> 01:01:29.210
Thank you all for what you do.

187
01:01:30.010 --> 01:01:32.090
You can give money to anything.

188
01:01:32.090 --> 01:01:33.450
You know, here’s another tip.

189
01:01:34.170 --> 01:01:36.890
When you walk through the city and a beggar comes up to you,

190
01:01:36.890 --> 01:01:37.850
you can do two things.

191
01:01:37.850 --> 01:01:43.690
You can easily rationalize it away and say that they are organized groups.

192
01:01:43.690 --> 01:01:45.130
Then you shouldn't give money.

193
01:01:45.130 --> 01:01:46.650
And of course, you need to have wisdom.

194
01:01:47.370 --> 01:01:49.450
Last week we were on vacation.

195
01:01:49.450 --> 01:01:52.650
Then a little guy came up to us while I was in line with the car.

196
01:01:52.650 --> 01:01:55.770
Then a little guy came up to me and he walked over with a bit of swag.

197
01:01:57.130 --> 01:01:59.610
With a Prada bag, wearing new sneakers.

198
01:01:59.610 --> 01:02:01.210
And he said, I'm poor, do you have money?

199
01:02:01.210 --> 01:02:02.570
I didn't give him any money.

200
01:02:02.570 --> 01:02:06.170
I thought to myself, come on, you're 18 years old, just go work at Kruidvat.

201
01:02:06.170 --> 01:02:07.770
You have to be smart, do you understand what I mean?

202
01:02:08.810 --> 01:02:14.810
Yes, yes, wait, so use wisdom, do you understand what I mean?

203
01:02:14.810 --> 01:02:22.890
But know that God lays it down as a law that we must give to the poor.

204
01:02:22.890 --> 01:02:26.570
And this is a universal law for all Christians.

205
01:02:26.570 --> 01:02:31.370
So the next time you go to Eindhoven or Hasselt,

206
01:02:31.370 --> 01:02:34.890
just put some Christmas money in your pocket.

207
01:02:35.290 --> 01:02:37.610
And if someone comes up to you, so that you...

208
01:02:37.610 --> 01:02:41.370
Because you know what my problem was at the border in Belgium?

209
01:02:41.370 --> 01:02:44.170
I had no cash on me, literally.

210
01:02:44.170 --> 01:02:48.730
I'm someone who loses everything that's in my pocket.

211
01:02:48.730 --> 01:02:51.690
So I never have cash on me.

212
01:02:51.690 --> 01:02:55.690
Yes, that guy obviously didn't have Pconic, he was really poor.

213
01:02:55.690 --> 01:02:57.770
And I said, sorry man, I have no money.

214
01:02:57.770 --> 01:02:59.530
Otherwise, I would have had to give him money.

215
01:02:59.530 --> 01:03:02.730
And I'm telling you this now and I'm telling it to the lady.

216
01:03:02.730 --> 01:03:03.690
I'm going to do this more often.

217
01:03:03.690 --> 01:03:07.210
When I'm in the city and someone asks for money,

218
01:03:07.210 --> 01:03:11.370
use your wisdom, speak with the Holy Spirit and just give ten euros.

219
01:03:11.370 --> 01:03:14.170
Just give 50 euros, just give 100 euros.

220
01:03:14.170 --> 01:03:16.010
And here is one thing I want to say.

221
01:03:16.010 --> 01:03:19.770
If it doesn't hurt, it's not a sacrifice.

222
01:03:19.770 --> 01:03:21.610
And that's just how it works.

223
01:03:21.610 --> 01:03:24.410
If it doesn't hurt, it's not a sacrifice.

224
01:03:24.410 --> 01:03:26.170
Sacrifices hurt.

225
01:03:26.170 --> 01:03:32.890
There is someone who can testify that sacrifices hurt.

226
01:03:32.890 --> 01:03:35.690
For he is suffering from a cross.

227
01:03:35.690 --> 01:03:39.610
So what is it, while we are on our way to Hasselt,

228
01:03:39.610 --> 01:03:42.250
because we want to buy a new polo shirt,

229
01:03:42.250 --> 01:03:45.850
what is 50 euros to someone who needs it?

230
01:03:45.850 --> 01:03:46.970
Do you understand what I mean?

231
01:03:46.970 --> 01:03:51.770
Let us be a church that lives sacrificially for the Lord.

232
01:03:51.770 --> 01:03:54.490
Carolien?

233
01:03:54.490 --> 01:03:55.610
Yes, I think that's pretty cool.

234
01:03:55.610 --> 01:03:58.890
Because we were recently on a camp with the youth, with the teenagers.

235
01:03:58.890 --> 01:04:00.810
And we were doing a city game there.

236
01:04:00.810 --> 01:04:02.330
So all kinds of fun, nice and pleasant.

237
01:04:02.410 --> 01:04:05.290
And at one point, it was warm,

238
01:04:05.290 --> 01:04:09.290
and we had gone into the supermarket to get something to drink and so on.

239
01:04:09.290 --> 01:04:12.410
And at one point, two of the teenagers said,

240
01:04:12.410 --> 01:04:13.690
well, there are two people there.

241
01:04:13.690 --> 01:04:17.370
And that woman was literally lying over the man's lap.

242
01:04:17.370 --> 01:04:19.290
And she seemed completely lifeless.

243
01:04:19.290 --> 01:04:25.610
And you could just see, yes, there was just nothing left in that man's eyes, so to speak.

244
01:04:25.610 --> 01:04:27.610
And she said, I want to go get something.

245
01:04:27.610 --> 01:04:30.410
So you went to get drinks with her own money,

246
01:04:30.410 --> 01:04:31.290
and to get something nice.

247
01:04:31.290 --> 01:04:31.930
And she had given that.

248
01:04:31.930 --> 01:04:33.770
And the man said, we have absolutely nothing.

249
01:04:33.770 --> 01:04:35.210
And he started to cry.

250
01:04:35.210 --> 01:04:38.010
And those girls were really touched.

251
01:04:38.010 --> 01:04:38.970
And then I said, you know what?

252
01:04:38.970 --> 01:04:40.330
I said, we're going to get something extra.

253
01:04:40.330 --> 01:04:41.770
So we went and got some nice food.

254
01:04:41.770 --> 01:04:45.450
And then one of the other teenagers said, I actually want to pray for those people.

255
01:04:45.450 --> 01:04:46.170
I said, that's fine.

256
01:04:46.170 --> 01:04:47.690
I said, then you can have this bag from me.

257
01:04:47.690 --> 01:04:48.810
And then you go and bring it.

258
01:04:48.810 --> 01:04:50.730
And go ask if you can pray.

259
01:04:50.730 --> 01:04:54.010
And those people, that man, he was completely crying.

260
01:04:54.010 --> 01:04:56.170
And that teenager prayed for him.

261
01:04:56.170 --> 01:04:58.570
And that bag of food was given.

262
01:04:58.570 --> 01:05:01.050
And everyone was taken aback.

263
01:05:01.050 --> 01:05:03.850
And completely emotional, because God was in it.

264
01:05:03.850 --> 01:05:04.330
So cool.

265
01:05:12.810 --> 01:05:16.490
Think about this during your prayers in the coming time.

266
01:05:16.490 --> 01:05:18.650
And make this a habit as a Christian.

267
01:05:18.650 --> 01:05:19.150
Amen.

268
01:05:19.690 --> 01:05:20.190
Amen.

269
01:05:20.490 --> 01:05:21.450
Shall we stand for a moment?

270
01:05:21.450 --> 01:05:23.450
I want to announce the Word of God.

271
01:05:23.450 --> 01:05:26.010
Vanessa will teach the Word of God today.

272
01:05:26.730 --> 01:05:33.850
And if you know Vanessa, I am sure she will encourage us about prayer.

273
01:05:33.850 --> 01:05:37.370
For my house shall be a house of prayer, says the Lord.

274
01:05:38.250 --> 01:05:40.650
And this is also part of the life of a Christian.

275
01:05:40.650 --> 01:05:42.730
And I want to ask you.

276
01:05:42.730 --> 01:05:43.850
Shall we close our eyes for a moment?

277
01:05:43.850 --> 01:05:47.450
For I want to pray for you, for this teaching that is coming.

278
01:05:47.450 --> 01:05:49.210
Can we all close our eyes?

279
01:05:49.210 --> 01:05:50.170
Let us pray together.

280
01:05:50.730 --> 01:05:51.930
Dear Father in heaven.

281
01:05:52.810 --> 01:05:56.650
As we just prayed at a quarter to ten before the start of this service,

282
01:05:56.650 --> 01:05:58.010
I want to pray again now.

283
01:05:58.010 --> 01:06:03.690
Holy Spirit, open our hearts to what you want to sow in our hearts today.

284
01:06:03.690 --> 01:06:08.410
Lord, if there are patterns of faith in our lives of comfort,

285
01:06:08.410 --> 01:06:12.330
that perhaps need to be released, release them at this moment.

286
01:06:12.330 --> 01:06:15.850
So that our hearts may be open to what your will is.

287
01:06:15.850 --> 01:06:18.970
Not our own patterns, our own habits,

288
01:06:18.970 --> 01:06:22.170
our own worldview and perspective.

289
01:06:22.170 --> 01:06:27.290
But that the kingdom of God may be sown at this moment through the Word of Vanessa.

290
01:06:27.290 --> 01:06:30.890
And we bless Vanessa in Jesus' mighty name.

291
01:06:30.890 --> 01:06:34.810
That her word from heaven will find its way into our hearts.

292
01:06:34.810 --> 01:06:36.090
In Jesus' name. Amen.

293
01:06:36.650 --> 01:06:37.050
Amen.

294
01:06:37.050 --> 01:06:37.690
Praise God.

295
01:06:37.690 --> 01:06:48.970
I will pray again if that’s okay.

296
01:06:48.970 --> 01:06:50.970
Let’s pray together.

297
01:06:50.970 --> 01:06:55.770
It is so difficult. Amen. It is so difficult to step out.

298
01:06:57.050 --> 01:06:59.530
One day it will be eternal. I have to keep telling myself that.

299
01:06:59.530 --> 01:07:00.890
One day. I must not come down.

300
01:07:00.890 --> 01:07:04.010
There will come a day when I may stay there forever.

301
01:07:04.010 --> 01:07:07.130
Lord, we love you.

302
01:07:07.130 --> 01:07:13.530
This is your house. It does not belong to us. It belongs to you.

303
01:07:14.250 --> 01:07:24.810
And I want to ask you. Lord, will you give us a revelation of that house today?

304
01:07:25.850 --> 01:07:36.570
Lord, that you build something that goes beyond walls.

305
01:07:37.610 --> 01:07:40.890
Floors and chairs. You are building something of eternal value.

306
01:07:40.890 --> 01:07:48.090
Lord, wake us up from that slumber.

307
01:07:48.090 --> 01:07:53.770
Give us a new understanding.

308
01:07:53.770 --> 01:08:05.850
A spirit of faith, revelation, and wisdom to walk in your way.

309
01:08:06.570 --> 01:08:16.330
Lord, I ask that you turn this house upside down and set it on fire.

310
01:08:16.330 --> 01:08:23.290
For we have not seen it yet. We have not touched it yet.

311
01:08:23.290 --> 01:08:32.890
But you want us. And you are leading us. So Lord, do your will. Amen.

312
01:08:33.210 --> 01:08:43.850
If you have a Bible with you, open it up.

313
01:08:43.850 --> 01:08:53.530
Matthew 21. Tomorrow evening the doors will open again for the house of prayer.

314
01:08:53.530 --> 01:08:57.770
We are always a house of prayer.

315
01:08:58.490 --> 01:09:01.930
At this moment we are a house of prayer.

316
01:09:01.930 --> 01:09:12.090
But we are a group that sacrifices itself.

317
01:09:12.090 --> 01:09:18.170
And now more than ever we need to be in prayer.

318
01:09:18.170 --> 01:09:25.130
It is important that we worship the Lord in spirit and in truth.

319
01:09:25.610 --> 01:09:36.410
The Bible does not leave the room when we worship Him.

320
01:09:36.410 --> 01:09:49.210
Some people get stirred up in the moment of a song, but they are not rooted in the Word.

321
01:09:49.210 --> 01:10:01.050
Some are deeply rooted in the Word, but do not know how to interact with the Spirit and in prayer.

322
01:10:01.050 --> 01:10:06.010
And the Lord always brings those two together.

323
01:10:06.010 --> 01:10:18.970
The Spirit loves the Word. He has written the Word. He desires the Word.

324
01:10:18.970 --> 01:10:20.970
And He reveals the Word.

325
01:10:31.930 --> 01:10:37.850
I want to give a piece of teaching today from the Word about prayer, which I have often addressed before.

326
01:10:37.850 --> 01:10:39.850
And that doesn't matter at all.

327
01:10:39.850 --> 01:10:54.810
Because I want to call us again to make a commitment to be part of that common house of prayer.

328
01:10:54.810 --> 01:11:10.810
And I want to blow away the idea that prayer is only for someone with a specific personality.

329
01:11:10.810 --> 01:11:15.770
That worship is a gift.

330
01:11:15.770 --> 01:11:21.770
That worship is for those who simply enjoy singing.

331
01:11:24.810 --> 01:11:28.810
Worship and prayer come through the disciples of God.

332
01:11:36.810 --> 01:11:42.810
The Lord will not return without sound. He returns on the sound of Judah, the praise here on earth.

333
01:11:42.810 --> 01:11:44.810
He is worthy.

334
01:11:44.810 --> 01:11:56.810
Those first 45 minutes are not for you or for me, but they are for the Lord.

335
01:12:04.810 --> 01:12:12.810
And there are so many new faces and I do not know where you come from, but here in Open Church, we believe the Bible.

336
01:12:12.810 --> 01:12:14.810
We teach from the Bible.

337
01:12:20.810 --> 01:12:24.810
And by the grace of God, we try to do that well. So pray for us.

338
01:12:28.810 --> 01:12:32.810
And we also believe in carrying out the Word.

339
01:12:36.810 --> 01:12:40.810
The kingdom is not a kingdom of hearing, it is a kingdom of doing.

340
01:12:42.810 --> 01:12:50.810
And if you receive teaching and you only hear it, but do not do it, then it leads to nothing.

341
01:12:54.810 --> 01:12:58.810
And until we do the Word of God, we do not live in the kingdom.

342
01:13:00.810 --> 01:13:02.810
That is what Tim just explained.

343
01:13:04.810 --> 01:13:08.810
There is a life of sacrifice for the disciple.

344
01:13:12.810 --> 01:13:14.810
And if we follow the land of the generations, we follow it.

345
01:13:26.810 --> 01:13:33.810
So I want to call us to make a new commitment to that house of prayer, to that corporate prayer.

346
01:13:33.810 --> 01:13:37.810
So Matthew 21, we know it, Jesus walking into the temple.

347
01:13:43.810 --> 01:13:50.810
And the story is about there being much selling and various things taking the place of the prayer room.

348
01:13:50.810 --> 01:13:52.810
And Jesus goes inside.

349
01:13:53.810 --> 01:14:00.810
And there is a lot going on there in that temple courtyard, buying and selling, and that takes the place where worship should have been.

350
01:14:01.810 --> 01:14:05.810
And again, if you are somewhere, you hear me teaching this, we have learned this extensively since 2020.

351
01:14:05.810 --> 01:14:11.810
But Jesus goes inside and he declares two scriptures, they are both prophets.

352
01:14:11.810 --> 01:14:18.810
And he declares that my house shall be called a house of prayer for all nations.

353
01:14:30.810 --> 01:14:33.810
My house shall be a house of prayer for all nations.

354
01:14:35.810 --> 01:14:37.810
That comes from Isaiah 56.

355
01:14:41.810 --> 01:14:44.810
So he walks into the house of his Father here on earth.

356
01:14:51.810 --> 01:14:58.810
God who became flesh, God himself walking here on earth enters the house of his Father.

357
01:15:00.810 --> 01:15:04.810
My house shall be called a house of prayer for all nations.

358
01:15:04.810 --> 01:15:05.810
That is what it is.

359
01:15:06.810 --> 01:15:11.810
And he speaks out, the house of my Father, my house, shall be a house of prayer for all nations.

360
01:15:13.810 --> 01:15:15.810
He gives a definition to that.

361
01:15:16.810 --> 01:15:17.810
He gives a purpose.

362
01:15:19.810 --> 01:15:21.810
That is the eternal purpose.

363
01:15:21.810 --> 01:15:24.810
2025, church leaders, pastors, flock.

364
01:15:28.810 --> 01:15:35.810
And church in 2025, do not change the definition that God Himself has given to His house.

365
01:15:37.810 --> 01:15:38.810
It is eternal.

366
01:15:39.810 --> 01:15:40.810
It still stands.

367
01:15:40.810 --> 01:15:45.810
You cannot change that, and if you do, you will find that it is destructive.

368
01:15:50.810 --> 01:15:54.810
And some of you have come here because other houses have been destroyed.

369
01:15:59.810 --> 01:16:06.810
And what I mean by that is that the spirit of the age allows to dictate what happens in the house of God.

370
01:16:10.810 --> 01:16:16.810
And what I mean by that is that the spirit of this time is given space to dictate what is going on in the house of God.

371
01:16:18.810 --> 01:16:19.810
And run away from those places.

372
01:16:19.810 --> 01:16:44.810
And in this house, we are trying, by the grace of God, to stay close to the spirit of God and to His Word, and we do not do that perfectly.

373
01:16:45.810 --> 01:16:46.810
But that is what we want.

374
01:16:49.810 --> 01:16:50.810
I am going in.

375
01:16:50.810 --> 01:16:54.810
But we have seen, unfortunately, that going home this year was not all a happy clap.

376
01:16:54.810 --> 01:16:58.810
There were some stories that broke my heart about the church.

377
01:16:59.810 --> 01:17:05.810
Going home to Australia was not just nice for me this year.

378
01:17:05.810 --> 01:17:10.810
There are stories about the houses of God there that have broken my heart.

379
01:17:10.810 --> 01:17:16.810
I said, Lord, how can this happen?

380
01:17:16.810 --> 01:17:30.810
How can the word of culture come in and the people who are supposed to minister from the Word of God, how can this happen?

381
01:17:30.810 --> 01:17:38.810
How can it happen that that culture from outside comes in so strongly that it dictates what will happen in a house of God?

382
01:17:38.810 --> 01:17:44.810
For do you know what the strange thing is? Everyone thinks they hear from God.

383
01:17:44.810 --> 01:17:54.810
God has changed His mind about everything and that is fine.

384
01:17:57.810 --> 01:18:11.810
God says, I am the same yesterday, today, and forever, and my beloved, you are the one who has changed.

385
01:18:11.810 --> 01:18:18.810
You need the transformation, I do not, God does not.

386
01:18:18.810 --> 01:18:29.810
To fit in His dwelling, to be fitting, to be in your place in that eternity.

387
01:18:29.810 --> 01:18:41.810
For in the kingdom now we must do those things that are also fitting in the kingdom to come.

388
01:18:48.810 --> 01:18:55.810
And you must engage in the struggle with everything in your life that does not fit in the kingdom now and the kingdom to come.

389
01:18:56.810 --> 01:18:59.810
Go read the mountain field again.

390
01:19:09.810 --> 01:19:19.810
In Matthew 5, 6, and 7, Jesus explains it so clearly. This is who you are and engage in the struggle with this. This is how you may become, stop that.

391
01:19:20.810 --> 01:19:26.810
I asked the Lord, but how does this happen? And His answer was prayer.

392
01:19:31.810 --> 01:19:35.810
Prayer full of fire, rooted in the Word, together.

393
01:19:35.810 --> 01:19:51.810
Cutting away what is flesh, cutting away what is the world, cutting away what is old and walking very narrowly in your life.

394
01:19:51.810 --> 01:19:58.810
For Jesus lays down here, this is my house, this is what it is, what it will be, and what it will become.

395
01:19:59.810 --> 01:20:10.810
And if you read in Jesus 56, then the context is when this kingdom goes worldwide, in which other kings will also enter the kingdom.

396
01:20:10.810 --> 01:20:21.810
And if you read in Isaiah 56, then the context is when this kingdom goes worldwide, in which other kings will also enter the kingdom.

397
01:20:21.810 --> 01:20:32.810
And if you read in Isaiah 56, then the context is when this kingdom goes worldwide, in which all the Gentile nations will come and bring their offerings to God.

398
01:20:40.810 --> 01:20:46.810
Isaiah the prophet 700 years before Jesus already sees, there will come a time that this will not only remain in Israel.

399
01:20:46.810 --> 01:20:56.810
That is where it started, that is where the center lies, that is where it will end, where He will return.

400
01:20:58.810 --> 01:21:00.810
Jerusalem is the city of the great king.

401
01:21:07.810 --> 01:21:14.810
In Zechariah we read that His feet will return to the Mount of Olives, and that is indeed where that Mount of Olives is.

402
01:21:16.810 --> 01:21:21.810
And God is the first who goes worldwide.

403
01:21:24.810 --> 01:21:29.810
God was the first to open it up to the ends of the earth.

404
01:21:46.810 --> 01:22:04.810
And Isaiah, in 700 BC, already prophesies that there will come a day when a sacrifice will be made that changes the whole planet, allowing everyone, even the Gentiles, to come.

405
01:22:07.810 --> 01:22:11.810
And that is the house of prayer for all nations.

406
01:22:12.810 --> 01:22:16.810
For every nation, for every tribe, for every language.

407
01:22:19.810 --> 01:22:21.810
And that is the culture of His house.

408
01:22:22.810 --> 01:22:24.810
It is the culture of His people.

409
01:22:24.810 --> 01:22:29.810
Prayer is not just an activity that we check off, it is not something on the agenda that starts tomorrow.

410
01:22:29.810 --> 01:22:31.810
Okay, I could do that, I could do that.

411
01:22:31.810 --> 01:22:35.810
It is the essential part of this whole thing.

412
01:22:36.810 --> 01:22:40.810
Prayer is the essential that carries all of this.

413
01:22:40.810 --> 01:22:45.810
It is not an agenda item that you can check off, but prayer permeates everything.

414
01:22:47.810 --> 01:22:48.810
Without prayer.

415
01:22:50.810 --> 01:22:52.810
Without worship for the Lord.

416
01:22:55.810 --> 01:22:58.810
That is where the fire goes out.

417
01:23:03.810 --> 01:23:07.810
This is where our hearts lose their connection and where we drift away.

418
01:23:08.810 --> 01:23:14.810
And then the house becomes a religious activity that people are part of, but not too much.

419
01:23:27.810 --> 01:23:31.810
While the Lord calls us to a sacrifice of praise.

420
01:23:31.810 --> 01:23:43.810
And the second quote that Jesus speaks when He walks into that temple courtyard comes from Jeremiah.

421
01:23:49.810 --> 01:23:53.810
He says, this is what it should have been, but you are making it a den of robbers.

422
01:23:57.810 --> 01:23:59.810
An interesting prophecy from Jeremiah.

423
01:24:02.810 --> 01:24:11.810
Jeremiah says that they should stand at the gates and tell the people entering the temple to change themselves.

424
01:24:11.810 --> 01:24:16.810
You come to the house, you do your thing, but you live as you want.

425
01:24:16.810 --> 01:24:19.810
And you think it is good.

426
01:24:20.810 --> 01:24:22.810
You think it is okay.

427
01:24:22.810 --> 01:24:24.810
That is what he says.

428
01:24:24.810 --> 01:24:25.810
That is Jeremiah 7.

429
01:24:32.810 --> 01:24:37.810
You come to the house of the Lord, but you live your own life and go your own way.

430
01:24:37.810 --> 01:24:38.810
Get away from here.

431
01:24:38.810 --> 01:24:40.810
Make sure you are changed.

432
01:24:45.810 --> 01:24:50.810
There comes a moment in your walk with God that the fleshly is no longer a problem.

433
01:24:52.810 --> 01:24:55.810
It is more about what is happening internally within you.

434
01:24:58.810 --> 01:25:00.810
It is more have I become apathetic.

435
01:25:02.810 --> 01:25:04.810
Have I become compliant.

436
01:25:06.810 --> 01:25:08.810
Am I becoming indifferent.

437
01:25:11.810 --> 01:25:12.810
God goes deeper with us.

438
01:25:13.810 --> 01:25:14.810
The first two, three years.

439
01:25:14.810 --> 01:25:17.810
Hopefully you have stopped having sex outside of marriage.

440
01:25:17.810 --> 01:25:19.810
You have stopped those crazy doubts.

441
01:25:19.810 --> 01:25:21.810
You have stopped with drinking too much, tasting too much.

442
01:25:21.810 --> 01:25:23.810
You have it, once again.

443
01:25:23.810 --> 01:25:25.810
You have the carnality.

444
01:25:25.810 --> 01:25:27.810
He shares with that first.

445
01:25:27.810 --> 01:25:33.810
In the first few years of your walk with God, I hope you have stopped cheating,

446
01:25:33.810 --> 01:25:40.810
with cursing, with all those fleshly oddities.

447
01:25:43.810 --> 01:25:45.810
But then he goes deeper.

448
01:25:46.810 --> 01:25:47.810
He wants more.

449
01:25:48.810 --> 01:25:50.810
He longs for everything.

450
01:25:51.810 --> 01:25:52.810
And that is everything.

451
01:25:53.810 --> 01:25:54.810
And he will not stop.

452
01:25:55.810 --> 01:25:56.810
Until he has your everything.

453
01:25:58.810 --> 01:26:00.810
He has completely given himself.

454
01:26:01.810 --> 01:26:02.810
And that is the example.

455
01:26:06.810 --> 01:26:10.810
He will not cease to chase after you, until he has you completely.

456
01:26:12.810 --> 01:26:13.810
And that is his grace.

457
01:26:20.810 --> 01:26:25.810
It is his grace that he does not leave us in a place where we are indifferent to him.

458
01:26:27.810 --> 01:26:29.810
One thing that it should not be.

459
01:26:30.810 --> 01:26:33.810
And I, once again, as we look at what...

460
01:26:33.810 --> 01:26:35.810
I do not know about all the churches here.

461
01:26:35.810 --> 01:26:38.810
I don't know where you come from and what they do.

462
01:26:38.810 --> 01:26:45.810
All I know is that you have come here because we have looked at death.

463
01:26:45.810 --> 01:26:48.810
We looked at what he wants as a priority.

464
01:26:48.810 --> 01:26:50.810
That is why you are here.

465
01:26:51.810 --> 01:26:53.810
And I don't know where you come from.

466
01:26:53.810 --> 01:26:59.810
But I do know that this is a place where we focus and prioritize praise and prayer.

467
01:26:59.810 --> 01:27:00.810
And that is why you are here.

468
01:27:00.810 --> 01:27:02.810
You may not know why you come here.

469
01:27:02.810 --> 01:27:04.810
But that is why you come here.

470
01:27:04.810 --> 01:27:06.810
For that is our purpose.

471
01:27:06.810 --> 01:27:07.810
That is our main purpose.

472
01:27:07.810 --> 01:27:09.810
To give him glory.

473
01:27:09.810 --> 01:27:10.810
To stay on the Word.

474
01:27:10.810 --> 01:27:12.810
To disciple him.

475
01:27:12.810 --> 01:27:16.810
And to make sure we do what he wants us to do.

476
01:27:24.810 --> 01:27:26.810
I believe, once again, in the robbing.

477
01:27:26.810 --> 01:27:27.810
What is the robbing about?

478
01:27:27.810 --> 01:27:29.810
So many houses are being robbed.

479
01:27:29.810 --> 01:27:31.810
So many houses have been stolen from.

480
01:27:33.810 --> 01:27:35.810
And they have been robbed of their glory.

481
01:27:38.810 --> 01:27:40.810
They have been robbed of their true purpose.

482
01:27:42.810 --> 01:27:44.810
Compromises have been made.

483
01:27:46.810 --> 01:27:48.810
Satisfaction has been taken.

484
01:27:53.810 --> 01:27:56.810
And the question is, how do we get out of this?

485
01:28:00.810 --> 01:28:04.810
And the only way out is to go back to what He has said.

486
01:28:09.810 --> 01:28:15.810
And if you read Scripture long enough, you will find that there are many repetitions in it.

487
01:28:19.810 --> 01:28:22.810
From A to Z, it is God who is calling us back.

488
01:28:22.810 --> 01:28:26.810
God always calls through prophetic voices and through people.

489
01:28:26.810 --> 01:28:28.810
He always says, come back to God.

490
01:28:33.810 --> 01:28:34.810
Come back.

491
01:28:36.810 --> 01:28:37.810
Come closer.

492
01:28:39.810 --> 01:28:41.810
Being close does too much.

493
01:28:48.810 --> 01:28:50.810
Do not stay in the forehead. Come closer.

494
01:28:51.810 --> 01:28:55.810
I have torn the veil so that you can enter the Holy of Holies.

495
01:29:00.810 --> 01:29:03.810
So many Christians and pastors are happy in that forehead.

496
01:29:05.810 --> 01:29:06.810
And I do not know why.

497
01:29:06.810 --> 01:29:10.810
For there is more with the Lord than just that forehead. Come closer. Go deeper. Enter into that glory.

498
01:29:24.810 --> 01:29:25.810
But it is confronting.

499
01:29:28.810 --> 01:29:30.810
Prayer is a confronting place.

500
01:29:32.810 --> 01:29:33.810
He will speak.

501
01:29:37.810 --> 01:29:40.810
The scary thing about prayer is that He actually speaks to us.

502
01:29:45.810 --> 01:29:49.810
And the fear that keeps people away is that they do not want to be touched too much by God.

503
01:29:56.810 --> 01:30:01.810
And yet the Lord says, come closer, for I have paid for so much more than what you are living in now.

504
01:30:03.810 --> 01:30:04.810
It is full of glory.

505
01:30:05.810 --> 01:30:06.810
It is good.

506
01:30:10.810 --> 01:30:13.810
You have the privilege of living close to the Lamb.

507
01:30:15.810 --> 01:30:16.810
To follow Him.

508
01:30:16.810 --> 01:30:21.810
And I understand that we are all at different points in our walk, but as a house there is a call to be closer.

509
01:30:38.810 --> 01:30:39.810
Jesus is our greatest example.

510
01:30:42.810 --> 01:30:43.810
He lived in personal prayer.

511
01:30:44.810 --> 01:30:45.810
Before the Father.

512
01:30:52.810 --> 01:30:56.810
He even said, I do nothing that I have not first seen the Father give to me.

513
01:30:59.810 --> 01:31:00.810
He lived with His disciples in prayer.

514
01:31:02.810 --> 01:31:03.810
He went to the temple.

515
01:31:05.810 --> 01:31:07.810
He was a regular guest at the temple.

516
01:31:07.810 --> 01:31:09.810
The communal place of worship and of the Word at that time.

517
01:31:19.810 --> 01:31:21.810
And He taught the disciples how they could pray.

518
01:31:22.810 --> 01:31:26.810
Because they saw the Lord when He was transfigured on the mountain of glory.

519
01:31:27.810 --> 01:31:28.810
He is in this glory.

520
01:31:28.810 --> 01:31:29.810
He has had prayer.

521
01:31:29.810 --> 01:31:30.810
And he is in this glory that shines.

522
01:31:31.810 --> 01:31:32.810
He is light.

523
01:31:32.810 --> 01:31:33.810
They said, we need to learn how to pray.

524
01:31:45.810 --> 01:31:46.810
Prayer is not a prayer list.

525
01:31:49.810 --> 01:31:50.810
Prayer is a person.

526
01:31:52.810 --> 01:31:53.810
Prayer is coming to the Lord.

527
01:31:57.810 --> 01:31:58.810
Prayer is unity with him.

528
01:32:02.810 --> 01:32:04.810
It is learning to see him as he truly is.

529
01:32:07.810 --> 01:32:08.810
It is learning to hear from him.

530
01:32:10.810 --> 01:32:11.810
And to do what he says.

531
01:32:13.810 --> 01:32:14.810
Prayer is confronting.

532
01:32:16.810 --> 01:32:17.810
I understand, it is really it.

533
01:32:18.810 --> 01:32:19.810
But if we do not go there.

534
01:32:26.810 --> 01:32:28.810
Then we will not receive the transformation we need either.

535
01:32:31.810 --> 01:32:32.810
I have seen that too often.

536
01:32:34.810 --> 01:32:35.810
We see it now.

537
01:32:39.810 --> 01:32:40.810
We see too many houses that are falling.

538
01:32:43.810 --> 01:32:44.810
And they do not stay close.

539
01:32:48.810 --> 01:32:50.810
Jesus was only able to complete his mission here on earth.

540
01:32:56.810 --> 01:32:58.810
Because he achieved victory in prayer in Gethsemane.

541
01:33:05.810 --> 01:33:06.810
He spent three hours in prayer that night.

542
01:33:12.810 --> 01:33:14.810
And he was alone and he asked his friends to support him.

543
01:33:18.810 --> 01:33:20.810
In the greatest test that Jesus had to endure, the cross.

544
01:33:21.810 --> 01:33:23.810
The sacrifice of his own life for the sake of the world.

545
01:33:25.810 --> 01:33:27.810
He is in prayer for three hours for the Father.

546
01:33:30.810 --> 01:33:31.810
Before he dies on the cross.

547
01:33:33.810 --> 01:33:35.810
He spends three hours in intense prayer with his Father.

548
01:33:39.810 --> 01:33:41.810
And we know that he asked his disciples to pray with him.

549
01:33:42.810 --> 01:33:43.810
And he still does that.

550
01:33:46.810 --> 01:33:48.810
He still asks his friends if they want to struggle with him in prayer.

551
01:33:54.810 --> 01:33:55.810
For he has not stopped praying.

552
01:33:57.810 --> 01:33:58.810
The ministry of the Lord continues in heaven.

553
01:34:03.810 --> 01:34:04.810
He is now the intercessor in heaven.

554
01:34:05.810 --> 01:34:06.810
He is far away, he has gone on.

555
01:34:07.810 --> 01:34:08.810
He prays for us.

556
01:34:08.810 --> 01:34:09.810
That we may come to him and be where he is.

557
01:34:17.810 --> 01:34:18.810
It says that he was in blood, sweat, and tears.

558
01:34:20.810 --> 01:34:21.810
That he prays.

559
01:34:22.810 --> 01:34:23.810
Through the cross.

560
01:34:24.810 --> 01:34:25.810
Gives his life.

561
01:34:25.810 --> 01:34:26.810
Not my will.

562
01:34:26.810 --> 01:34:27.810
Your will be done.

563
01:34:27.810 --> 01:34:28.810
Oh my.

564
01:34:28.810 --> 01:34:29.810
Not my will.

565
01:34:29.810 --> 01:34:30.810
Am I going to do it?

566
01:34:30.810 --> 01:34:31.810
Not my will.

567
01:34:31.810 --> 01:34:32.810
I am going to do it.

568
01:34:32.810 --> 01:34:33.810
I am going to do it.

569
01:34:33.810 --> 01:34:34.810
I am going to do it.

570
01:34:34.810 --> 01:34:35.810
I am going to do it.

571
01:34:35.810 --> 01:34:36.810
I am going to do it.

572
01:34:36.810 --> 01:34:37.810
I am going to do it.

573
01:34:37.810 --> 01:34:38.810
I am going to do it.

574
01:34:39.810 --> 01:34:40.810
I am going to do it.

575
01:34:40.810 --> 01:34:41.810
I am going to do it.

576
01:34:42.810 --> 01:34:43.810
I am going to do it.

577
01:34:43.810 --> 01:34:44.810
I am going to do it.

578
01:34:45.810 --> 01:34:46.810
I am going to do it.

579
01:35:02.810 --> 01:35:03.810
And Christians see that they can live with Christ.

580
01:35:03.810 --> 01:35:07.810
And then we think as Christians that we can live with Christ without prayer.

581
01:35:10.810 --> 01:35:11.810
This is not how it works, church.

582
01:35:18.810 --> 01:35:23.810
There is too much flesh, too much hidden sin in the house of God, and in Jeremiah we read that he knows that.

583
01:35:26.810 --> 01:35:30.810
You cannot live from proximity forever.

584
01:35:33.810 --> 01:35:38.810
You cannot be part of a house, leave during worship, and think that God does not know that.

585
01:35:46.810 --> 01:35:47.810
You need prayer.

586
01:35:49.810 --> 01:35:51.810
You need a life of prayer.

587
01:35:54.810 --> 01:35:56.810
Not my will here, Your will.

588
01:36:00.810 --> 01:36:02.810
It was not easy to come back this time.

589
01:36:04.810 --> 01:36:08.810
I never left my country because I did not like it there.

590
01:36:11.810 --> 01:36:12.810
I follow the Lord.

591
01:36:13.810 --> 01:36:14.810
It is not easy.

592
01:36:16.810 --> 01:36:18.810
There are challenges time and again.

593
01:36:27.810 --> 01:36:29.810
For in my flesh I cannot do this.

594
01:36:29.810 --> 01:36:34.810
So my prayer remains, Lord help me, not my will.

595
01:36:36.810 --> 01:36:37.810
Pray that more.

596
01:36:42.810 --> 01:36:48.810
Some of you have been here for decades, but you have never prayed, Lord not my will.

597
01:36:59.810 --> 01:37:12.810
And we need each other in this, so seek people out, pray together, come to the house of prayer, we need each other.

598
01:37:17.810 --> 01:37:19.810
There is an expectation to pray.

599
01:37:22.810 --> 01:37:24.810
Leaders, we expect you to pray.

600
01:37:30.810 --> 01:37:34.810
And I am not trying to present a nice story, but this is what it is, we expect you to pray.

601
01:37:42.810 --> 01:37:44.810
If you lead a lifegroup, be in prayer.

602
01:37:48.810 --> 01:37:52.810
Don't be an island unto yourself, come to that communal house of prayer.

603
01:37:55.810 --> 01:37:58.810
We need to come together in prayer.

604
01:37:59.810 --> 01:38:08.810
On Sunday mornings at a quarter to ten, leaders, teams, if you are active, come and pray.

605
01:38:19.810 --> 01:38:22.810
Our priority is to pray and that expectation is there as well.

606
01:38:22.810 --> 01:38:29.810
It is difficult to call others to things we ourselves do not do.

607
01:38:33.810 --> 01:38:37.810
It is difficult to cultivate things in others that we ourselves do not care about.

608
01:38:38.810 --> 01:38:43.810
That applies to everything, that applies to prayer, that applies to giving financially, that applies to serving, that applies to everything we do.

609
01:38:43.810 --> 01:38:47.810
We cannot call it forth or explain it without living it ourselves, it is impossible.

610
01:38:55.810 --> 01:38:58.810
But if the church stops praying,

611
01:39:01.810 --> 01:39:04.810
then they let the robber in.

612
01:39:04.810 --> 01:39:07.810
And then they quickly become that culture of the world.

613
01:39:13.810 --> 01:39:16.810
And we are gatekeepers for the house of God.

614
01:39:16.810 --> 01:39:19.810
My role is to set you in prayer. I cannot call you this morning.

615
01:39:19.810 --> 01:39:22.810
Some of you will go outside and not listen, that's okay.

616
01:39:22.810 --> 01:39:25.810
That is on you. I say, my role is to do that.

617
01:39:25.810 --> 01:39:28.810
As long as I have to be here, I must do that for you.

618
01:39:28.810 --> 01:39:31.810
But it is up to you what you do with God.

619
01:39:31.810 --> 01:39:34.810
This is your life with God.

620
01:39:34.810 --> 01:39:37.810
This is to encourage you to be part of that prayer.

621
01:39:37.810 --> 01:39:40.810
And I cannot force you, you can walk out and do what you want,

622
01:39:40.810 --> 01:39:43.810
but you will continue to receive that encouragement from me.

623
01:40:05.810 --> 01:40:09.810
This is our role as watchmen. It is so important that we pray.

624
01:40:09.810 --> 01:40:12.810
It is of eternal value and it is not about a good feeling,

625
01:40:12.810 --> 01:40:15.810
or a cozy moment, or a nice encouragement.

626
01:40:17.810 --> 01:40:20.810
That is part of the problem.

627
01:40:21.810 --> 01:40:24.810
If the church is about having a nice moment.

628
01:40:29.810 --> 01:40:32.810
You are all looking on, when will she stop?

629
01:40:33.810 --> 01:40:36.810
But I want to eat.

630
01:40:36.810 --> 01:40:39.810
And this is spiritual food.

631
01:40:55.810 --> 01:40:59.810
When you read the book of Joel, the prophet Joel,

632
01:40:59.810 --> 01:41:02.810
you see how God deals with things.

633
01:41:02.810 --> 01:41:05.810
There is a crisis in the land and God does not go to the government.

634
01:41:08.810 --> 01:41:11.810
He goes directly to the spiritual leaders.

635
01:41:12.810 --> 01:41:15.810
And he says, pray.

636
01:41:15.810 --> 01:41:18.810
You have left the altar.

637
01:41:20.810 --> 01:41:23.810
You have stopped being a watchman.

638
01:41:24.810 --> 01:41:27.810
You have leaned back in the house of God.

639
01:41:34.810 --> 01:41:37.810
And if the leadership leans back, how can they bring in the flock?

640
01:41:37.810 --> 01:41:40.810
That will not work.

641
01:41:53.810 --> 01:41:56.810
You are so drunk on culture.

642
01:41:56.810 --> 01:41:59.810
You miss the new wine, the spiritual wine.

643
01:41:59.810 --> 01:42:02.810
And the revelation of Jesus Christ in your life.

644
01:42:02.810 --> 01:42:05.810
That is what happens, church.

645
01:42:17.810 --> 01:42:20.810
We need to get drunk.

646
01:42:21.810 --> 01:42:24.810
In the Holy Spirit.

647
01:42:26.810 --> 01:42:29.810
We need to be under the influence.

648
01:42:30.810 --> 01:42:33.810
But not of the world.

649
01:42:34.810 --> 01:42:37.810
Not of what the world offers us to drink.

650
01:42:40.810 --> 01:42:43.810
Be drunk in the Holy Spirit of God.

651
01:42:43.810 --> 01:42:46.810
And join Him.

652
01:42:46.810 --> 01:42:49.810
And enjoy that.

653
01:42:49.810 --> 01:42:52.810
There will be joy in the house of prayer.

654
01:42:52.810 --> 01:42:55.810
That is what He promises.

655
01:43:02.810 --> 01:43:05.810
But He says, you give it away.

656
01:43:05.810 --> 01:43:08.810
You enjoy the world.

657
01:43:08.810 --> 01:43:11.810
You dance to a different melody.

658
01:43:12.810 --> 01:43:15.810
You are not pure, you are not holy.

659
01:43:15.810 --> 01:43:18.810
You do not walk in my purpose.

660
01:43:18.810 --> 01:43:21.810
You lose the reward that I have prepared for you.

661
01:43:31.810 --> 01:43:34.810
I am not necessarily talking about being saved.

662
01:43:34.810 --> 01:43:37.810
But being saved is being saved to that glory.

663
01:43:37.810 --> 01:43:40.810
There is more than just being saved.

664
01:43:40.810 --> 01:43:43.810
And then dancing with the world for another 50 years.

665
01:43:53.810 --> 01:43:56.810
We have entered a building.

666
01:44:02.810 --> 01:44:05.810
I forwarded this to the worship team.

667
01:44:05.810 --> 01:44:08.810
It says, you are in a church. Please be quiet.

668
01:44:11.810 --> 01:44:14.810
I agree with the second part. Dress a little appropriately.

669
01:44:23.810 --> 01:44:26.810
But I said it to the worship team.

670
01:44:26.810 --> 01:44:29.810
This is not exactly our message.

671
01:44:31.810 --> 01:44:34.810
We do the Bible.

672
01:44:34.810 --> 01:44:37.810
Sing a new song for the Lord.

673
01:44:37.810 --> 01:44:40.810
Shout for the Lord.

674
01:44:40.810 --> 01:44:43.810
All the earth.

675
01:44:46.810 --> 01:44:49.810
Make music with cymbals and on the lyre.

676
01:44:49.810 --> 01:44:52.810
And on the piano and the electric guitar.

677
01:44:52.810 --> 01:44:55.810
This will be the house of prayer in every nation.

678
01:44:55.810 --> 01:44:58.810
Until he returns.

679
01:44:58.810 --> 01:45:01.810
Every language, every people, every tribe.

680
01:45:01.810 --> 01:45:04.810
Will let their sound be heard.

681
01:45:04.810 --> 01:45:07.810
This is a house of prayer.

682
01:45:07.810 --> 01:45:10.810
I want to put forward the suggestion.

683
01:45:10.810 --> 01:45:13.810
I want to put forward the suggestion.

684
01:45:13.810 --> 01:45:16.810
I want to put forward the suggestion.

685
01:45:16.810 --> 01:45:19.810
I want to put forward the suggestion.

686
01:45:20.810 --> 01:45:23.810
I want to put forward the suggestion that this is the problem.

687
01:45:28.810 --> 01:45:31.810
Culture dictates a church that is silent.

688
01:45:32.810 --> 01:45:35.810
Church, keep your mouth shut.

689
01:45:35.810 --> 01:45:38.810
Do not tell your people that they will not sin.

690
01:45:39.810 --> 01:45:42.810
That is so easy.

691
01:45:43.810 --> 01:45:46.810
Listen to me.

692
01:45:46.810 --> 01:45:49.810
This is the kingdom.

693
01:45:50.810 --> 01:45:53.810
In this house, we expect you to transform.

694
01:46:02.810 --> 01:46:05.810
Sometimes it is difficult.

695
01:46:05.810 --> 01:46:08.810
We have been at it for 9 years.

696
01:46:08.810 --> 01:46:11.810
When we talk to you face-to-face...

697
01:46:11.810 --> 01:46:14.810
Everything is going up.

698
01:46:14.810 --> 01:46:17.810
Overall, it is okay.

699
01:46:17.810 --> 01:46:20.810
But when we address you one-on-one...

700
01:46:20.810 --> 01:46:23.810
Don't touch me.

701
01:46:23.810 --> 01:46:26.810
I'm in the house of God.

702
01:46:26.810 --> 01:46:29.810
We want to transform you.

703
01:46:29.810 --> 01:46:32.810
We have seen it.

704
01:46:32.810 --> 01:46:35.810
It is glorious and good.

705
01:46:36.810 --> 01:46:39.810
We have seen it happen.

706
01:46:39.810 --> 01:46:42.810
People are coming to the Lord.

707
01:46:42.810 --> 01:46:45.810
They are in love with Jesus.

708
01:46:45.810 --> 01:46:48.810
They are being filled with the Spirit.

709
01:46:48.810 --> 01:46:51.810
They are getting a hunger for God in prayer.

710
01:46:51.810 --> 01:46:54.810
They hear Him.

711
01:46:54.810 --> 01:46:57.810
This is how our lives should look.

712
01:46:57.810 --> 01:47:00.810
This is the problem.

713
01:47:00.810 --> 01:47:03.810
If we do not give glory...

714
01:47:04.810 --> 01:47:07.810
If we do not give that glory...

715
01:47:08.810 --> 01:47:11.810
Then we stray from the path.

716
01:47:19.810 --> 01:47:22.810
In Romans 1 you see that happening.

717
01:47:22.810 --> 01:47:25.810
They turned away from God.

718
01:47:25.810 --> 01:47:28.810
They forgot to give Him praise.

719
01:47:28.810 --> 01:47:31.810
They went off their path.

720
01:47:33.810 --> 01:47:36.810
If you are serving...

721
01:47:36.810 --> 01:47:39.810
Call your people and your team.

722
01:47:39.810 --> 01:47:42.810
When you are serving...

723
01:47:42.810 --> 01:47:45.810
Then you must be a corporate company.

724
01:47:45.810 --> 01:47:48.810
When you are serving...

725
01:47:48.810 --> 01:47:51.810
Then you must provide for your companies.

726
01:47:51.810 --> 01:47:54.810
You must provide for your companies.

727
01:47:54.810 --> 01:47:57.810
You must provide for your companies.

728
01:47:57.810 --> 01:48:00.810
Your companies change.

729
01:48:01.810 --> 01:48:04.810
Serving does not always change.

730
01:48:04.810 --> 01:48:07.810
Prayer changes things.

731
01:48:11.810 --> 01:48:14.810
You can hide in serving for 30 years...

732
01:48:14.810 --> 01:48:17.810
and in prayer you will be confronted.

733
01:48:20.810 --> 01:48:24.810
In this time of history, prayer must increase, not decrease.

734
01:48:24.810 --> 01:48:27.810
Jesus said...

735
01:48:27.810 --> 01:48:30.810
In place of prayer, the greatest thing you will receive...

736
01:48:30.810 --> 01:48:33.810
my spirit that is in you.

737
01:48:37.810 --> 01:48:40.810
Prayer is like a container for the spirit.

738
01:48:42.810 --> 01:48:45.810
Prayer is the way the Holy Spirit works.

739
01:48:49.810 --> 01:48:52.810
Without prayer, there is also no continuous filling with the spirit.

740
01:48:55.810 --> 01:48:58.810
We see this so clearly in Acts.

741
01:48:59.810 --> 01:49:02.810
The Spirit falls during a prayer meeting.

742
01:49:03.810 --> 01:49:06.810
The beginning of the church is a prayer gathering.

743
01:49:07.810 --> 01:49:10.810
But that is not the end of the church.

744
01:49:10.810 --> 01:49:13.810
Nor the end of prayer.

745
01:49:19.810 --> 01:49:22.810
Prayer is the power that makes the church bold.

746
01:49:22.810 --> 01:49:25.810
It is the connection with the head.

747
01:49:25.810 --> 01:49:28.810
The connection with the one we love.

748
01:49:30.810 --> 01:49:33.810
If the body is not connected to the head...

749
01:49:33.810 --> 01:49:36.810
nothing can flow there.

750
01:49:41.810 --> 01:49:44.810
The early church is constantly in prayer and worship.

751
01:49:44.810 --> 01:49:47.810
There is a powerful movement of the gospel.

752
01:49:48.810 --> 01:49:51.810
The two go hand in hand.

753
01:49:53.810 --> 01:49:56.810
Why is the gospel not preached with power and courage?

754
01:49:57.810 --> 01:50:00.810
Because there is no prayer.

755
01:50:03.810 --> 01:50:06.810
For those prayer meetings are the backbone of preaching the gospel.

756
01:50:17.810 --> 01:50:20.810
The more I live in prayer, the more I also feel the Spirit filling me...

757
01:50:20.810 --> 01:50:23.810
when it is time to distribute.

758
01:50:23.810 --> 01:50:26.810
And if there is a disconnect, I feel that very quickly.

759
01:50:30.810 --> 01:50:33.810
Prayer is the carrier of God's power. He fills it.

760
01:50:38.810 --> 01:50:41.810
If you do not feel the power of the Spirit, come to prayer.

761
01:50:45.810 --> 01:50:48.810
It doesn't take years to lose that connection. It takes days.

762
01:50:50.810 --> 01:50:53.810
I have been in prayer for a few days. I feel the disconnect.

763
01:50:53.810 --> 01:50:56.810
I need God's prayer meetings.

764
01:50:56.810 --> 01:50:59.810
I cannot do it in my body, but neither can you.

765
01:51:08.810 --> 01:51:11.810
We have learned a lot this year in the first and second Chronicles.

766
01:51:11.810 --> 01:51:14.810
The tabernacle of David is now the blueprint for the house of prayer on earth.

767
01:51:20.810 --> 01:51:23.810
That is the layout for what we are doing now.

768
01:51:30.810 --> 01:51:33.810
It is the musical song and the prayer that is rooted in the Word.

769
01:51:39.810 --> 01:51:42.810
God sought the heart of His people.

770
01:51:43.810 --> 01:51:46.810
He has given us His Son.

771
01:51:46.810 --> 01:51:49.810
And now the only cause that remains is the cause of the price.

772
01:51:54.810 --> 01:51:57.810
It is musical prayer and the prayer that the Lord has appointed.

773
01:52:00.810 --> 01:52:03.810
This is His choice.

774
01:52:03.810 --> 01:52:06.810
To be appointed for all eternity on behalf of His people.

775
01:52:12.810 --> 01:52:15.810
This is His choice.

776
01:52:15.810 --> 01:52:18.810
This is how He moves.

777
01:52:19.810 --> 01:52:22.810
As it is in heaven, let it also be here on earth.

778
01:52:26.810 --> 01:52:29.810
When we sing here on earth, it reminds of the house in heaven.

779
01:52:34.810 --> 01:52:37.810
And He draws us there.

780
01:52:37.810 --> 01:52:40.810
Where there is price and prayer...

781
01:52:42.810 --> 01:52:45.810
There the Lord is drawn to.

782
01:52:47.810 --> 01:52:50.810
That reminds him of that heavenly throne.

783
01:52:53.810 --> 01:52:56.810
He feels at home there.

784
01:53:02.810 --> 01:53:05.810
That house of David and also the tabernacle now is in a time of darkness.

785
01:53:07.810 --> 01:53:10.810
It is situated like a city of light on the hill.

786
01:53:14.810 --> 01:53:17.810
He wants light in his house. He wants prayer in his house.

787
01:53:20.810 --> 01:53:23.810
It stands in the middle of the cause.

788
01:53:23.810 --> 01:53:26.810
The house of God stands in the middle of the cause.

789
01:53:29.810 --> 01:53:32.810
The cause for survival.

790
01:53:38.810 --> 01:53:41.810
And he says, I want my people to glorify me through the power of my spirit.

791
01:53:53.810 --> 01:53:56.810
It is not by might. It is not by power.

792
01:53:56.810 --> 01:53:59.810
But it is by the power of the spirit in your midst.

793
01:54:00.810 --> 01:54:03.810
We are going to make a commitment to the Lord.

794
01:54:17.810 --> 01:54:20.810
We do it not because it is easy or because there are no other things to do.

795
01:54:20.810 --> 01:54:23.810
We do it because this really matters.

796
01:54:24.810 --> 01:54:27.810
If you are too busy to pray in your personal life, then you are too busy.

797
01:54:35.810 --> 01:54:38.810
If you are too busy to be part of that collective prayer, then you are too busy.

798
01:54:43.810 --> 01:54:46.810
Everyone is busy, but we need to make room.

799
01:54:47.810 --> 01:54:50.810
Do not keep making excuses.

800
01:54:56.810 --> 01:54:59.810
So dedicate yourself and make that promise.

801
01:55:02.810 --> 01:55:05.810
Give offering.

802
01:55:08.810 --> 01:55:11.810
I want to give you a few practical things.

803
01:55:12.810 --> 01:55:15.810
On Monday evenings we come together here from half past seven to nine.

804
01:55:20.810 --> 01:55:23.810
And that has been going on for about four or five years now.

805
01:55:26.810 --> 01:55:29.810
You can come for the whole hour and a half. You can also join for half an hour.

806
01:55:29.810 --> 01:55:32.810
Just come in.

807
01:55:34.810 --> 01:55:37.810
You don't have to be on time. Just come whenever you can.

808
01:55:42.810 --> 01:55:45.810
We let the Word of the Lord out. We let the glory of God out.

809
01:55:45.810 --> 01:55:48.810
I am not asking for an audience.

810
01:55:48.810 --> 01:55:51.810
It is not for the glory of the team.

811
01:55:51.810 --> 01:55:54.810
I say, we will do it anyway.

812
01:55:54.810 --> 01:55:57.810
But your coming in is part of our letting out.

813
01:55:57.810 --> 01:56:00.810
The sound of the glory that the gospel will explode in a region.

814
01:56:02.810 --> 01:56:05.810
It is not up to us, it is up to His glory.

815
01:56:05.810 --> 01:56:08.810
But this is how He operates.

816
01:56:11.810 --> 01:56:14.810
But it is about giving glory to the Lord that He deserves.

817
01:56:14.810 --> 01:56:17.810
And whether we are two or two hundred.

818
01:56:17.810 --> 01:56:20.810
We will magnify the Lord at that time.

819
01:56:23.810 --> 01:56:26.810
And I promise you it will change you.

820
01:56:30.810 --> 01:56:33.810
The first Monday of the month is for all leaders and all teams.

821
01:56:33.810 --> 01:56:36.810
Please be there.

822
01:56:42.810 --> 01:56:45.810
We want to come together on that first Monday of the month.

823
01:56:45.810 --> 01:56:48.810
And also pray for each other and for the ministry and for whatever the Lord lays on our hearts.

824
01:56:48.810 --> 01:56:51.810
For families, divide.

825
01:56:51.810 --> 01:56:54.810
Tell one person one evening, the other person the next evening.

826
01:56:54.810 --> 01:56:57.810
Be creative.

827
01:56:57.810 --> 01:57:00.810
See how you can fit it in.

828
01:57:00.810 --> 01:57:03.810
Do you have distance?

829
01:57:03.810 --> 01:57:06.810
Be creative.

830
01:57:06.810 --> 01:57:09.810
See how you can fit it in.

831
01:57:09.810 --> 01:57:12.810
Do you have distance?

832
01:57:12.810 --> 01:57:15.810
Be creative.

833
01:57:15.810 --> 01:57:18.810
Be creative.

834
01:57:18.810 --> 01:57:21.810
See how you can fit it in.

835
01:57:21.810 --> 01:57:24.810
Do you have older children?

836
01:57:24.810 --> 01:57:27.810
Take them with you.

837
01:57:27.810 --> 01:57:30.810
Make it a family evening.

838
01:57:30.810 --> 01:57:33.810
Bring your Bible.

839
01:57:33.810 --> 01:57:36.810
Pray.

840
01:57:36.810 --> 01:57:39.810
Write.

841
01:57:39.810 --> 01:57:42.810
Sing.

842
01:57:43.810 --> 01:57:46.810
We always start with a time of magnifying the Lord.

843
01:57:51.810 --> 01:57:55.810
We magnify Him with songs we know and songs straight from the heart.

844
01:57:57.810 --> 01:58:00.810
Songs from the spirit.

845
01:58:02.810 --> 01:58:06.810
And as a collective group, we do this together as well.

846
01:58:07.810 --> 01:58:10.810
You can pray in the spirit.

847
01:58:28.810 --> 01:58:34.810
And there are moments, there are evenings when we ask to come together in groups of 2 or 3 to pray for specific topics.

848
01:58:37.810 --> 01:58:40.810
Always say Amen.

849
01:58:40.810 --> 01:58:43.810
Don't leave each other hanging.

850
01:58:43.810 --> 01:58:46.810
Don't let each other dry out.

851
01:58:46.810 --> 01:58:49.810
And when you pray together, then agree with one another.

852
01:58:49.810 --> 01:58:52.810
Say Amen.

853
01:58:52.810 --> 01:58:55.810
Let that flow be there.

854
01:58:55.810 --> 01:58:58.810
On every last day of the month, we have intercession.

855
01:58:58.810 --> 01:59:01.810
We pray for here and for Israel.

856
01:59:01.810 --> 01:59:04.810
I want you to get a heart for that.

857
01:59:07.810 --> 01:59:11.810
Then we come together, and those are truly intercession evenings.

858
01:59:11.810 --> 01:59:16.810
We pray for this region, we pray for Israel, and I really want to warm you up for that.

859
01:59:22.810 --> 01:59:26.810
And we pray that the will of the Lord will be done here on earth.

860
01:59:29.810 --> 01:59:32.810
And we pray from the Word, we are rooted in the Word.

861
01:59:37.810 --> 01:59:40.810
And this is also a way to get to know who God is.

862
01:59:40.810 --> 01:59:43.810
For you pray from His Word, you pray His will, and you get to know Him better through that.

863
01:59:59.810 --> 02:00:02.810
And I want to ask you to make a commitment.

864
02:00:07.810 --> 02:00:11.810
And I want to invite you to make an appointment with the Lord.

865
02:00:11.810 --> 02:00:15.810
And just to say, Lord, this is what I want to give to you in prayer this year.

866
02:00:20.810 --> 02:00:23.810
Appointments are biblical.

867
02:00:23.810 --> 02:00:26.810
So let's take a moment for that while the band plays.

